.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_CREATE_MPQE 3 2026-09-04 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_create_mpqe \- create an MPQE-wrapped MPQ archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_create_mpqe("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s **" "archive,"
.BI "        const char     *" "path,"
.BI "        const uint8_t  *" "auth_code,"
.BI "        size_t          " "auth_code_size,"
.BI "        const mpq_archive_create_options_s *" "options"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a new MPQE stream containing an MPQ v1 or v2 archive. The caller
supplies at least 32 authentication-code bytes. Add members using the
ordinary writer APIs; \fBlibmpq__archive_close\fP() finalizes the archive,
encrypts it, and atomically publishes the result on success.
.SS "Creation Options"
Compression defaults to STANDARD. Add
LIBMPQ_ARCHIVE_CREATE_COMPRESSION_EXTENDED to options.flags to select
EXTENDED. The policy affects writer validation only, not decoding.
.SS "Optional Attributes"
Set options.attributes to a combination of LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_CRC32,
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_FILETIME, LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_MD5, and
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_PATCH_BIT. Zero disables generation; any nonzero
combination creates one (attributes) file and consumes one reserved slot.
Unknown attribute bits are rejected. Version-100 attributes work in both
MPQ v1 and v2, independently of the archive format version.
.PP
Capacity includes the attributes entry and listfile if enabled; the internal
attributes name is reserved. Finalization writes the listfile, attributes,
then the completed tables. Checksums cover source bytes before compression.
FILETIME defaults to zero and patch bits are zero. Use
\fBlibmpq__writer_timestamp\fP() on an active writer for an explicit
timestamp. Path addition never imports filesystem timestamps.
.SS "Temporary Storage and Publication"
The normal writer first finalizes a private temporary plaintext MPQ in the
destination directory, then encrypts it for publication. The plaintext
temporary file is owner-only; the completed MPQE archive uses normal output
permissions determined by the caller's umask.
.PP
Existing MPQE archives cannot be modified. Cleanup is best effort, so a
crash can leave an owner-only plaintext temporary file behind.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success or a negative LIBMPQ_ERROR_* code. Missing or short
authentication data returns LIBMPQ_ERROR_DECRYPT.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__archive_attributes (3),
.BR libmpq__file_attributes (3),
